~ blamed
if Utils.character.get_trust() >= 6 and Utils.character.get_interest() >= 2 and not Utils.ctx["is_suspicious"]
	Silvia: I see.
	Silvia: So all that careful questioning was merely theatre.
	Silvia: Your diagnostic conclusion represents catastrophic intellectual failure.
	Silvia: I provided empirical transparency, yet you defaulted to prosecuting cold composure because emotional suspects make you nervous.
elif Utils.ctx["is_pressured"] or Utils.ctx["is_suspicious"] or Utils.character.get_trust() <= -4
	Silvia: Predictable.
	Silvia: You have been leaning toward me for some time.
	Silvia: I cannot say your conclusion is well-supported, but it is at least consistent.
elif Utils.ctx["family_focus"] >= 3
	Silvia: Of course.
	Silvia: Inheritance. Bloodline. Resentment.
	Silvia: You prefer motives that arrange themselves neatly.
elif Utils.ctx["evidence_focus"] >= 9 and Utils.ctx["blame"] < 3
	Silvia: That surprises me.
	Silvia: Your evidence was better than this conclusion.
	Silvia: Somewhere, you abandoned your own method.
elif Utils.ctx["is_stressed"] or Utils.ctx["is_confused"]
	Silvia: You are exhausted.
	Silvia: This is what exhaustion does. It mistakes closure for proof.
else
	Silvia: Then say it plainly.
	Silvia: If you are going to accuse me, at least do me the courtesy of not dressing impulse as reason.
=> END
